<!--meta {"lead": "Inline messages sit right next to what they describe: a hint under a field, the error that says how to fix it, a quiet Saved beside a form.", "description": "Field hint, field error, character counter and inline status (neutral, success, warning, danger), in both themes.", "pills": ["Linked with <code>aria-describedby</code>", "Status: stable"], "variants": "field hint, field error, counter, inline status (neutral, success, warning, danger), live dot", "states": "hint, invalid, over limit, saving, saved, failed", "sources": ["pages/booking-request/invalid", "pages/account-settings/invalid", "pages/reset-password/invalid", "dialogs/filter-braiders/invalid", "pages/booking-request/submitting", "pages/account-settings/submitting", "pages/account-settings/success", "pages/account-settings/failed"]} -->
<section class="ds-section" id="overview"><h2><a href="#overview">Overview</a></h2>
  <p>Use an inline message for feedback that belongs to one control or one small area, placed where the eye already is. Use an <a href="alert.html">alert</a> for a condition that affects a region or the page (and the error summary that lists every invalid field), and a <a href="toast.html">toast</a> for feedback about an action that has finished elsewhere.</p>
  <ul>
    <li><b>Field hint</b> (<code>.field__help</code>): what to enter, shown before anyone makes a mistake: "Use at least 12 characters."</li>
    <li><b>Field error</b> (<code>.field__error</code>): what is wrong and how to fix it, shown after validation.</li>
    <li><b>Counter</b> (<code>.field__counter</code>): characters used against a limit, under a review textarea.</li>
    <li><b>Inline status</b> (<code>.inline-status</code>): a short state beside a form or row: "Saving…", "Saved just now", "Not saved".</li>
  </ul>
</section>

<section class="ds-section" id="anatomy"><h2><a href="#anatomy">Anatomy</a></h2>
  <div class="ds-anatomy">
    <figure class="ds-anatomy__figure">
      <div class="field" style="width: 100%;"><label class="field__label" for="anatomy-email">Email</label><input class="input" id="anatomy-email" type="email" value="maya.chen@example" aria-invalid="true" aria-describedby="anatomy-email-error"><span class="field__error" id="anatomy-email-error">Enter an email address like name@example.com.</span></div>
      <span class="ds-callout" style="left: 2%; top: 74%;" aria-hidden="true">1</span>
      <span class="ds-callout" style="left: 40%; top: 74%;" aria-hidden="true">2</span>
      <span class="ds-callout" style="left: 90%; top: 46%;" aria-hidden="true">3</span>
    </figure>
    <ol class="ds-anatomy__list">
      <li><div><b>Warning glyph (errors)</b><small>Generated "⚠" with empty alternative text, so it is not read aloud; pairs the colour with a shape.</small></div></li>
      <li><div><b>Message</b><small>Body small, <code>--color-danger-fg</code> for errors and <code>--color-fg-muted</code> for hints; 4px under the control.</small></div></li>
      <li><div><b>Link to the control</b><small>The message's <code>id</code> is in the control's <code>aria-describedby</code>; errors also set <code>aria-invalid="true"</code>.</small></div></li>
    </ol>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="ds-section" id="variants"><h2><a href="#variants">Variants</a></h2>
  {{example:[stack]Hint before input, error after validation, counter on a textarea.}}
<div class="field"><label class="field__label" for="var-password">New password</label><input class="input" id="var-password" type="password" autocomplete="new-password" aria-describedby="var-password-help"><span class="field__help" id="var-password-help">Use at least 12 characters.</span></div>
<div class="field"><label class="field__label" for="var-time">Preferred time</label><input class="input" id="var-time" type="text" value="Sat 24 Oct, 7:00 am" aria-invalid="true" aria-describedby="var-time-error"><span class="field__error" id="var-time-error">Choose an offered time. Nia starts at 9:00 am on Saturdays.</span></div>
<div class="field"><label class="field__label" for="var-review">Your review</label><textarea class="textarea" id="var-review" aria-describedby="var-review-count">Nia explained each step and the braids feel comfortable.</textarea><span class="field__counter" id="var-review-count">56 of 500 characters</span></div>
  {{/example}}
  {{example:Inline status beside an action; the live dot pulses only while work is in progress.}}
<span class="inline-status" role="status"><span class="dot dot--pulse" aria-hidden="true"></span>Saving…</span>
<span class="inline-status inline-status--success" role="status">{{icon:check|icon--sm}}Saved just now</span>
<span class="inline-status inline-status--warning">{{icon:warning|icon--sm}}Saved on this device only</span>
<span class="inline-status inline-status--danger">{{icon:alert-circle|icon--sm}}Not saved</span>
  {{/example}}
</section>

<section class="ds-section" id="sizes" data-na="Inline messages use the body-small size everywhere so they stay subordinate to the control they describe."><h2><a href="#sizes">Sizes</a></h2></section>

<section class="ds-section" id="states"><h2><a href="#states">States</a></h2>
  <p>Messages are not interactive; their state follows the control and the data. The control's own hover and focus states are shown for context.</p>
  <div class="ds-matrix"><table>
    <thead><tr><th scope="col">Variant</th><th scope="col">Default</th><th scope="col">Control focused</th><th scope="col">Invalid</th><th scope="col">Disabled control</th></tr></thead>
    <tbody>
      <tr><th scope="row">Hint</th><td><div class="field"><label class="field__label" for="st-1">Phone</label><input class="input" id="st-1" type="tel" value="416-555-0148" aria-describedby="st-1-h"><span class="field__help" id="st-1-h">Braiders text this number.</span></div></td><td><div class="field"><label class="field__label" for="st-2">Phone</label><input class="input" id="st-2" type="tel" value="416-555-0148" data-state="focus" aria-describedby="st-2-h"><span class="field__help" id="st-2-h">Braiders text this number.</span></div></td><td><div class="field"><label class="field__label" for="st-3">Phone</label><input class="input" id="st-3" type="tel" value="416-555" aria-invalid="true" aria-describedby="st-3-e st-3-h"><span class="field__error" id="st-3-e">Enter a 10-digit phone number.</span><span class="field__help" id="st-3-h">Braiders text this number.</span></div></td><td><div class="field"><label class="field__label" for="st-4">Phone</label><input class="input" id="st-4" type="tel" value="416-555-0148" disabled aria-describedby="st-4-h"><span class="field__help" id="st-4-h">Verify your email to change this.</span></div></td></tr>
      <tr><th scope="row">Counter</th><td><div class="field"><label class="field__label" for="st-5">Your review</label><textarea class="textarea" id="st-5" aria-describedby="st-5-c">The parts were so neat.</textarea><span class="field__counter" id="st-5-c">23 of 500 characters</span></div></td><td><div class="field"><label class="field__label" for="st-6">Your review</label><textarea class="textarea" id="st-6" data-state="focus" aria-describedby="st-6-c">The parts were so neat.</textarea><span class="field__counter" id="st-6-c">23 of 500 characters</span></div></td><td><div class="field"><label class="field__label" for="st-7">Your review</label><textarea class="textarea" id="st-7" aria-invalid="true" aria-describedby="st-7-c">…</textarea><span class="field__counter" id="st-7-c" data-over="true">512 of 500 characters</span></div></td><td>—</td></tr>
      <tr><th scope="row">Inline status</th><td><span class="inline-status"><span class="dot dot--pulse" aria-hidden="true"></span>Saving…</span></td><td><span class="inline-status inline-status--success">{{icon:check|icon--sm}}Saved just now</span></td><td><span class="inline-status inline-status--danger">{{icon:alert-circle|icon--sm}}Not saved</span></td><td><span class="inline-status inline-status--warning">{{icon:warning|icon--sm}}Saved on this device only</span></td></tr>
    </tbody>
  </table></div>
  <h3>Both themes</h3>
  {{themes:stack}}<span class="field__help">Use at least 12 characters.</span><span class="field__error">Enter an email address like name@example.com.</span><span class="inline-status inline-status--success">{{icon:check|icon--sm}}Saved just now</span><span class="inline-status inline-status--warning">{{icon:warning|icon--sm}}Saved on this device only</span><span class="inline-status inline-status--danger">{{icon:alert-circle|icon--sm}}Not saved</span>{{/themes}}
  <ul>
    <li><b>Timing</b>: an error first shows after a submit attempt, or once the control has been changed and left; it then re-validates on every input so it disappears as soon as the value is fixed (the form field owns this timing).</li>
    <li><b>Hint plus error</b>: keep the hint; put the error first in <code>aria-describedby</code> so it is read first.</li>
    <li><b>Over limit</b>: <code>data-over="true"</code> turns the counter danger and the textarea invalid; never truncate what was typed.</li>
  </ul>
</section>

<section class="ds-section" id="responsive"><h2><a href="#responsive">Responsive behaviour</a></h2>
  <ul>
    <li>Messages wrap under their control at any width; they never sit beside it, so they cannot overflow at 360px.</li>
    <li>In two-column form rows (768px and up), each field keeps its own message; rows align to the top so a long error does not push its neighbour.</li>
    <li>Inline status wraps below the form's actions on phones.</li>
    <li>A word longer than the line, such as "name@example.com" at 200% text on a 360px screen, breaks (<code>overflow-wrap: anywhere</code>) instead of overflowing the field.</li>
  </ul>
</section>

<section class="ds-section" id="theming"><h2><a href="#theming">Theming</a></h2>
  <p>Hints read <code>--color-fg-muted</code>, errors and over-limit counters <code>--color-danger-fg</code>, counters <code>--color-fg-subtle</code>, and status tones their <code>--color-*-fg</code>. In dark mode the danger text lightens to red-300 so it stays above 4.5:1 on grey-900.</p>
  <pre><code>/* Hints inside a dialog keep the dialog's muted colour */
.dialog .field__help { color: var(--color-fg-muted); }</code></pre>
</section>

<section class="ds-section" id="accessibility"><h2><a href="#accessibility">Accessibility</a></h2>
  <h3>Role and pattern</h3>
  <p>Plain text tied to its control with <code>aria-describedby</code>; errors add <code>aria-invalid="true"</code> to the control. Inline status that changes after load sits in a <code>role="status"</code> element so "Saved just now" is announced politely. The message lives outside the <code>&lt;label&gt;</code>, so it is not part of the field's name.</p>
  <h3>Keyboard</h3>
  <table class="ds-table ds-keys"><thead><tr><th scope="col">Key</th><th scope="col">Action</th></tr></thead><tbody>
    <tr><td><kbd>Tab</kbd></td><td>Focus goes to the control; its hint or error is read as its description. Messages are never focusable.</td></tr>
  </tbody></table>
  <h3>Focus</h3>
  <p>On a failed submit, focus moves to the error summary, whose links move focus into each invalid field; the inline error is then read with the field.</p>
  <h3>Labelling</h3>
  <p>Errors name the problem and the fix in the field's terms ("Enter a 10-digit phone number"). The "⚠" glyph has empty alternative text (<code>content: "⚠" / ""</code>). Counters say "of 500 characters", not just "23/500".</p>
  <h3>Contrast</h3>
  <div class="ds-example__canvas ds-example__canvas--stack" style="padding: 0; gap: var(--space-2);">
    {{pair:Hint on card|--color-fg-muted|--color-bg-surface|4.5}}
    {{pair:Error on card|--color-danger-fg|--color-bg-surface|4.5}}
    {{pair:Error on page|--color-danger-fg|--color-bg-canvas|4.5}}
    {{pair:Counter on card|--color-fg-subtle|--color-bg-surface|4.5}}
    {{pair:Success status on card|--color-success-fg|--color-bg-surface|4.5}}
    {{pair:Warning status on card|--color-warning-fg|--color-bg-surface|4.5}}
  </div>
  <h3>Motion</h3>
  <p>Messages appear without animation. The live dot pulses over <code>--duration-loop-pulse</code> only while work is in progress, and pauses at full opacity under reduced motion (<code>--motion-loop-state</code>). Use the dot, not a spinner, beside a busy button: the button already shows the spinner.</p>
  <h3>Touch</h3>
  <p>Not a target. Keep errors directly under the field so they are visible above the on-screen keyboard.</p>
</section>

<section class="ds-section" id="content"><h2><a href="#content">Content</a></h2>
  <ul>
    <li>Errors are one sentence: what to do, with an example when the format is unclear: "Enter an email address like name@example.com."</li>
    <li>Never blame ("You entered an invalid value") and never be vague ("Enter a valid value to continue").</li>
    <li>Hints explain constraints before they bite: "Use at least 12 characters."</li>
    <li>Status is a few words (five at most), past tense for done: "Saved just now", "Not saved", "Saved on this device only"; an ellipsis for work in progress: "Saving…".</li>
  </ul>
</section>

<section class="ds-section" id="do-dont"><h2><a href="#do-dont">Do and don't</a></h2>
  <div class="ds-dodont">
    <figure class="ds-do"><div class="ds-example__canvas ds-example__canvas--stack"><div class="field"><label class="field__label" for="dd-time">Preferred time</label><input class="input" id="dd-time" type="text" value="Sat 24 Oct, 7:00 am" aria-invalid="true" aria-describedby="dd-time-error"><span class="field__error" id="dd-time-error">Choose an offered time. Nia starts at 9:00 am on Saturdays.</span></div></div><figcaption>The error sits outside the label and says how to fix it.</figcaption></figure>
    <figure class="ds-dont"><div class="ds-example__canvas ds-example__canvas--stack"><label class="field" for="dd-bad"><span class="field__label">Rating, 1 to 5</span><input class="input" id="dd-bad" type="number" value="7" aria-invalid="true"><span class="field__error">Enter a valid value to continue.</span></label></div><figcaption>The error nested inside the <code>&lt;label&gt;</code> becomes part of the field's name, and the copy is vague (the mocks' default error).</figcaption></figure>
    <figure class="ds-do"><div class="ds-example__canvas ds-example__canvas--stack"><div class="field"><label class="field__label" for="dd-pw">New password</label><input class="input" id="dd-pw" type="password" autocomplete="new-password" aria-describedby="dd-pw-help"><span class="field__help" id="dd-pw-help">Use at least 12 characters.</span></div></div><figcaption>Tell people the rule before they submit.</figcaption></figure>
    <figure class="ds-dont"><div class="ds-example__canvas ds-example__canvas--stack"><div class="field"><label class="field__label" for="dd-pw2">New password</label><input class="input" id="dd-pw2" type="password" autocomplete="new-password"></div></div><figcaption>The password rule only appears as an error after a failed attempt (reset-password invalid).</figcaption></figure>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="ds-section" id="tokens"><h2><a href="#tokens">Tokens</a></h2>
  <div class="ds-table-wrap"><table class="ds-table">
    <thead><tr><th scope="col">Part</th><th scope="col">Token</th><th scope="col">Light</th><th scope="col">Dark</th></tr></thead>
    <tbody>
      {{tok:Hint|--color-fg-muted}}
      {{tok:Error and over-limit counter|--color-danger-fg}}
      {{tok:Counter|--color-fg-subtle}}
      {{tok:Status success / warning|--color-success-fg|--color-warning-fg}}
      {{tok:Invalid control edge|--color-danger-solid}}
      {{tok:Message font / counter font|--text-body-sm|--text-caption}}
      {{tok:Gap from control / icon gap|--space-1|--space-2}}
      {{tok:Pulse cycle|--duration-loop-pulse}}
    </tbody>
  </table></div>
</section>

<section class="ds-section" id="code"><h2><a href="#code">Code</a></h2>
  <pre><code>&lt;div class="field"&gt;
  &lt;label class="field__label" for="email"&gt;Email&lt;/label&gt;
  &lt;input class="input" id="email" type="email" aria-invalid="true" aria-describedby="email-error email-help"&gt;
  &lt;span class="field__error" id="email-error"&gt;Enter an email address like name@example.com.&lt;/span&gt;
  &lt;span class="field__help" id="email-help"&gt;Braiders use this to confirm.&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;span class="inline-status inline-status--success" role="status"&gt;…Saved just now&lt;/span&gt;</code></pre>
  <table class="ds-table"><thead><tr><th scope="col">Class / attribute</th><th scope="col">Effect</th></tr></thead><tbody>
    <tr><td><code>.field__help</code></td><td>Hint under a control.</td></tr>
    <tr><td><code>.field__error</code></td><td>Error with the warning glyph.</td></tr>
    <tr><td><code>.field__counter</code> + <code>data-over="true"</code></td><td>Character counter; danger colour when over the limit.</td></tr>
    <tr><td><code>.inline-status</code> + <code>--success|--warning|--danger</code></td><td>Inline state text with an icon or dot.</td></tr>
    <tr><td><code>.dot</code> <code>.dot--pulse</code></td><td>Status dot; pulse while in progress.</td></tr>
    <tr><td><code>aria-describedby</code> / <code>aria-invalid</code></td><td>Tie the message to its control; mark the control invalid.</td></tr>
  </tbody></table>
</section>

<section class="ds-section" id="sources"><h2><a href="#sources">Sources</a></h2>
  <p>Extracted from these mocks:</p>
  <ul>
    {{mock:pages/booking-request/invalid|"Choose a time Nia offers. Her first slot on Sat 24 Oct is 10:00 am."}}
    {{mock:pages/account-settings/invalid|email format error}}
    {{mock:pages/reset-password/invalid|password length error}}
    {{mock:dialogs/filter-braiders/invalid|error inside a dialog}}
    {{mock:pages/booking-request/submitting|"Sending your request to Nia…" status beside the busy button}}
    {{mock:pages/account-settings/submitting|"Saving…" status beside the busy button}}
    {{mock:pages/account-settings/success|"Saved just now" success status}}
    {{mock:pages/account-settings/failed|"Not saved" danger status}}
  </ul>
  <p>Drift fixed during extraction: the error <code>&lt;span&gt;</code> was nested inside the <code>&lt;label class="field"&gt;</code>, making it part of the field's accessible name (system: <code>div.field</code> with <code>label for</code> and the error outside); the "⚠" glyph was read aloud (now empty alternative text); the fallback error "Enter a valid value to continue." was vague; no field had a hint, so rules such as the 12-character password appeared only as errors; the hint, counter and inline-status variants were added from the core set.</p>
</section>
